# NEOCOM Git conventions

Primary owner: `/neocom-git`. Detail skill: `/neocom-git-workflow`. `/neo:pr` commits and prepares pull requests for one project, or for every repository when no project is given.

## Commits

```text
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

<optional body — why>

<optional footer>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `style`, `perf`, `revert`  
Scopes (examples): `front`, `meta`, `back`, `openspec`, `root`, `infra`, `login`, `init`

- Imperative mood; body explains **why**
- HEREDOC for `git commit -m`; no secrets
- Commit only when asked, when `/neo:pr` is invoked, or when `/neocom-git` is invoked to commit
- No amend unless user rules allow; no force push to main/master; never update git config

## PRs

- `gh pr create` with **Summary** + **Test plan**
- Push `-u` when needed; title mirrors conventional style or branch purpose
- Name the repository and any OpenSpec changes
- Do not update a submodule pointer. `neocom` is deprecated

## Releases

- Branches: `feat/…` (or `feature/…` when user-mandated), `fix/…`, `release/x.y.z`; tags: `vX.Y.Z`
- On a new **`neocom-front`** `feature/…` branch, first set GitVersion `MajorMinorPatch` in `package.json`, both `appVersion` env fields, and the `index.html` loading message
- Checklist: tests green, OpenSpec status noted, release stays in the owning repository
- Align with L2 `INFRA-036`…`INFRA-039`; do not invent undeclared deploy targets
